{number: 20}
{title: Jesus Is All the World to Me}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Jesus is all the world to me, my [Db] life, my joy, my [Ab] all;
He is my strength from day to day, with-[Eb] out Him I would [Ab] fall.
When I am sad to [Fm] Him I go, no [Db] other one can [Eb] cheer me so;
When [Ab] I am sad He makes me glad, He’s [Db] my [Eb] Fri-[Ab] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Jesus is all the world to me, my [Db] Friend in trials [Ab] sore;
I go to Him for blessings, and He [Eb] gives them o’er and [Ab] o’er.
He sends the sunshine [Fm] and the rain, He [Db] sends the harvest’s [Eb] golden grain;
Sun-[Ab] shine and rain, harvest of grain, He’s [Db] my [Eb] Fri-[Ab] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Jesus is all the world to me, and [Db] true to Him I’ll [Ab] be;
O, how could I this Friend deny, when [Eb] He’s so true to [Ab] me?
Following Him I [Fm] know I’m right, He [Db] watches o’er me [Eb] day and night;
Fol-[Ab] lowing Him by day and night, He’s [Db] my [Eb] Fri-[Ab] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Ab] Jesus is all the world to me, I [Db] want no better [Ab] friend;
I trust Him now, I’ll trust Him when life’s [Eb] fleeting days shall [Ab] end.
Beautiful life with [Fm] such a Friend; beau-[Db] tiful life that [Eb] has no end;
E-[Ab] ternal life, eternal joy, He’s [Db] my [Eb] Fri-[Ab] end.
{end_of_verse}
